# Fix: Broken Thumbnails in Chatbot Project Cards

## Context

The chatbot at josephibrahim.com renders inline project cards when the AI references a project (via `[PROJECT:slug]` markers). These cards show a thumbnail, title, client, and a link arrow. The problem: 10 of 11 projects have `thumbnail: ''` (empty string) in `lib/projects.ts`, so the `<img src="">` renders as a broken image icon with alt text visible.

Screenshot shows "Apple Vision Pro" and "iPhone 14 Pro Max" cards with broken image placeholders.

## Approach: Conditionally Hide Thumbnail

Rather than populating all 11 thumbnail URLs (many projects don't have readily available Vimeo thumbnails), make the card gracefully handle missing thumbnails by simply not rendering the image container when `thumbnail` is empty.

This is the minimal, correct fix -- no new dependencies, no placeholder images, no layout shift.

## Changes

### 1. `components/ChatProjectCard.tsx` (lines 49-69)

Wrap the thumbnail `<div>` in a conditional: only render when `project.thumbnail` is truthy.

```tsx
// Before (always renders img, broken when empty):
<div style={{ width: '80px', ... }}>
  <img src={project.thumbnail} ... />
</div>

// After (skip thumbnail entirely when empty):
{project.thumbnail && (
  <div style={{ width: '80px', ... }}>
    <img src={project.thumbnail} ... />
  </div>
)}
```

The card layout already uses flexbox with `gap: 16px`, so removing the thumbnail div will just shift the title/client leftward -- clean and intentional.

### 2. Performance note (`transition: all`)

The card has `transition: 'all 0.2s ease'` on line 38. Per Vercel best practices (`rerender-` rules), this should be `transition: 'background-color 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease'` since only those two properties change on hover. This is a minor fix but worth doing while we're in this file.

